-- title:
--   Build the complete local cover from uninitialized workspace
-- statement:
--   Fix $h\in\mathbb N$, let $L=512h$, local prime $p$, vertex count $V=\binom Lh$, candidate count $R=p^{2L}$, and schedule length $T$. Reserve ordered areas for $V$ masks, $VL$ bits, $2LR$ coefficients, two $2V$ raw arrays, two $Rp$ histograms, an $Rp^2$ matrix, scratch $z$, and $2LT$ schedule coefficients at $a\ge z+p^2+R+T$.
--
--   Assume the specified enumeration, bit-table, and cover-host procedures. Their defined build word budget fits $W$, the candidate workspace and output fit $S\le W$, and $d+L+7\le D$. Without assumptions on the initial contents of these areas, execution establishes
--   $$r=a,\qquad\text{correct candidate tables, covering matrix, greedy indices, and scheduled weight rows}.$$
--   It takes the mask-enumeration time, bit-table time, and local-cover host time plus $200$, and preserves all memory preceding the mask area.
--
--   This closes the local-cover construction by producing its own finite graph representation before selecting the schedule.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/LightLocalCoverBuild.lean#L51-L138

